WHOAMI(1)                      User Commands                       WHOAMI(1)

NAME
    whoami, id - show your login identity

SYNOPSIS
    whoami
    id

DESCRIPTION
    Print the uid the kernel attests for this login; id prints the group
    as well. The identity is fixed when you log in. The shell cannot change
    it and a program cannot claim another: every check the fs_server makes
    is against what the kernel says, not what a client asserts.

SEE ALSO
    sudo(1), passwd(1)
